trong>PUNE</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>2</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>10</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>SECUNDERABAD</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>2</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>3</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>VADODARA</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>0</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>3</strong></p></td></tr></tbody></table><table><tbody><tr><td colspan="5"><p><strong><br>V. Mid Career Training Details</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Sl.No</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Year</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Training Name</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Period</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Institute Name</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1.</p></td><td><p>Nil</p></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table><table><tbody><tr><td colspan="7"><p><strong>VI. In-Service Training Details</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Sl.No</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Year</strong></p></td><td colspan="2"><p><strong>Training Name</strong></p></td><td colspan="2"><p><strong>Period</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Institute Name</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p>1.</p></td><td><p>2002</p></td><td colspan="2"><p>Role of Br. A.O in-Charge in Computerized Functioning</p></td><td colspan="2"><p>22.09.02 to 24.09.02</p></td><td><p>RTC, Kolkata</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2.</p></td><td><p>2009</p></td><td colspan="2"><p>-</p></td><td colspan="2"><p>17.08.09 to 2108.09</p></td><td><p>Admn. Staff College, Hyderabad</p></td></tr><tr><td colspan="7"><p><strong>VII. Domestic Training Details</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Sl.No</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Year</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Training Name</strong></p></td><td colspan="2"><p><strong>Period</strong></p></td><td colspan="2"><p><strong>Institute Name</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td colspan="2"></td><td colspan="2"></td></tr></tbody></table><table><tbody><tr><td colspan="5"><p><strong>VIII. Foreign Training Details</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Sl.No</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Year</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Training Name</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Period</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Country</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td><p>Nil</p></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr><tr><td><p>A</p></td><td colspan="3"><ol><li>Whether Debarred from Foreign Training?</li><li>If so, period of debarment</li></ol></td><td><p>No</p></td></tr></tbody></table><table><tbody><tr><td colspan="4"><p><strong>IX. Award / Publication Details</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td><p><strong>Sl.No</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Date &amp;Year</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Particulars in brief</strong></p></td><td><p><strong>Institution</strong></p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>', 'D:\Admin_Sharing\CDA Sect\43 Shri T Rambabu CDA-ER Sheet.docx', false, 1);
INSERT INTO public.document_pages VALUES (7, 6, '2026-07-03', 1, 'Imported Page 1', '<p><strong>DO Letter No. DO/ITSDC/TR							Date: 17.07.2025</strong></p><p><strong>From:</strong><br>Shri T Rambabu, IDAS<br>Controller of Defence Accounts (IT&amp;SDC)<br>CDA (ITS&amp;DC), Secunderabad – 500015</p><p><strong>To:</strong><br>Shri Dhananjay Kumar, IDAS<br>Principal Controller of Defence Accounts<br>PCDA, New Delhi – 110001</p><p><strong>Subject:</strong> Request for visit of PCDA, New Delhi along with team to CDA (ITS&amp;DC), Secunderabad to address development issues related to integration into ‘Tulip’ application – reg.</p><p><strong>Dear Shri Dhananjay Kumar,</strong></p><p>I am writing to kindly request your visit, along with your team, to the office of CDA (ITS&amp;DC), Secunderabad in connection with the ongoing development activities and resolution of technical issues pertaining to the integration of PCDA New Delhi into the ‘Tulip’ application.</p><p>As you are aware, the successful integration of PCDA New Delhi into the ‘Tulip’ platform is crucial for achieving uniformity in processes and operational efficiency. However, certain development and functional challenges have been observed, which require detailed discussions and joint resolution efforts in coordination with the development team stationed at ITS&amp;DC, Secunderabad.</p><p>In this regard, I would request you to kindly consider visiting CDA (ITS&amp;DC), Secunderabad, along with your team, at an early and mutually convenient date. This visit will facilitate focused discussions with the development team, enable on-the-spot resolution of pending issues, and help expedite the smooth onboarding of PCDA New Delhi into the ‘Tulip’ system.</p><p>Your kind cooperation and support in this matter will be highly appreciated.</p><p>With warm regards,</p><p>Yours sincerely,</p><p><br><strong>T Rambabu, IDAS</strong><br><strong>CDA (ITS&amp;DC)</strong><br>CDA (ITS&amp;DC), Secunderabad – 500015</p><p><strong>DO Letter No. DO/ITSDC/TR							Date: 17.07.2025</strong></p><p><strong>Dear Shri Dhananjay Kumar,</strong></p><p>	You are aware that ITSDC, Secunderabad is tasked with development activities and resolution of technical issues pertaining to integration of PCDA New Delhi into ‘Tulip’ application.</p><p>	Successful integration of PCDA New Delhi into the ‘Tulip’ platform is crucial for achieving uniformity in processes and operational efficiency. However, certain development and functional challenges have been observed which require detailed discussions and joint resolution efforts in coordination with the development team stationed at ITS&amp;DC, Secunderabad.</p><p>	Therefore, I would request you to kindly consider visiting CDA (ITS&amp;DC), Secunderabad, along with your team, at an early and mutually convenient date. This visit will facilitate focused discussions with the development team, enable on-the-spot resolution of pending issues, and help expedite the smooth on boarding of PCDA New Delhi into the ‘Tulip’ system.</p><p><strong>	</strong></p><p><strong>											Yours </strong></p><p>To,</p><p>	Shri Dhananjay Kumar, IDAS<br>	Principal Controller of Defence Accounts<br>	PCDA, New Delhi – 110001</p><p>IT&amp;SDC/SysMisc/Dolphin/7cpc 	  	                   				 		   .08.2025.</p><p>Dear</p><p>	Consequent to Review Meeting held on 24.07.2025 chaired by the then Special CGDA Shri R.K. Arora IDAS, on categorisation of pending Samanvyay issues pertaining to Dolphin, this office had identified seven audit related issues and were included in the Annexure to our office email dated 28.07.2025 seeking clarifications which are still awaited.  A copy of the same is attached herewith for your ready reference.</p><p>	 </p><p>2.	I request your personal attention in expediting clarifications with regard to all the points, in particular regarding  updated/revised location code details from IHQ for adjustment of field allowances, RISK/HAUCA in respect of JCOs/ORs including Honorary Commissioned Officers of the Army so as to enable this office for taking appropriate action and for resolution of pending Samanvyay issues.  I would be grateful for an early action in the matter.</p><p>	With</p><p>											</p><p>												Yours</p><p>Smt. Richa Misra, IDAS</p><p>Joint CGDA (Audit),</p><p>O/o. CGDA,</p><p>Ulan Batar Road,</p><p>Delhi Cantt. 110010.</p><p>IFA/12/2025-26		 			  			 	         Oct, 2025.</p><p>Dear</p><p>	This has reference to HQrs letter No. IFA/10/STT&amp;LTT/2025-26 dated: 02.09.2025 regarding furnishing a Quarterly Report on IFA matters.</p><p>2.	Procedural issues observed during the scrutiny of cases are being communicated to the Units for corrective action and for optimum utilization of resources. Guidelines received from HQrs Office are being disseminated to Units and cases are examined accordingly to safeguard the interest of the state and to ensure accountability.</p><p>3.	Interaction with Executive Authorities is a regular activity and aimed at resolving pending issues, if any.</p><p>4.	The requisite data, in prescribed format, is enclosed as Annexure ‘A’ to this DO letter. </p><p>	With</p><p>											</p><p>										Yours</p><p>Shri Vishvajit Sahay, IDAS</p><p>Special CGDA,</p><p>O/o. CGDA,</p><p>Ulan Batar Road, Palam,</p><p>Delhi Cantt. 110 010.</p>', 'D:\Admin_Sharing\CDA Sect\DO.docx', false, 1);
INSERT INTO public.document_pages VALUES (8, 7, '2026-07-03', 1, 'Imported Page 1', '<p><strong>Annexure – B</strong></p><p><strong>Changes in Tulip 2.0</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>S.No</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Functionalities in Tulip 2.0</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Current Status</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Technology Stack Upgrade</p></td><td><p>Tulip has been upgraded from Seam 2.2 to a modern, industry-standard stack using <strong>React JS and Spring Boot</strong>, delivering improved performance, scalability, and maintainability.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Hosting process and Tulip architecture: </p></td><td><p>Hosting will be done in <strong>centralized</strong> way.<br>[3 models were discussed (Decentralized, Hybrid, Centralized)].</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Centralized Master Data Management</p></td><td><p>Earlier, offices maintained separate local tables for Units, Vendors, and Bank details. These have now been unified into <strong>Central Unit, Vendor, and Bank Masters</strong>, providing a single authoritative data source and ensuring seamless integration, consistency, and easier maintenance across all offices.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>Role-Based Authentication</p></td><td><p>Existing activity-based authentication required mapping each user to individual activities. Tulip 2.0 replaces this with a streamlined <strong>role-based</strong> authentication system, simplifying user management and improving access control, security, and scalability.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Implementation of 14 digit unique unit code for all departmental applications.</p></td><td><p>A <strong>14-digit FIS code</strong>, already used in the existing Tulip system, has now been integrated into Tulip 2.0 also.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Redesigning R Section role; data capture at dak diarisation (bill intake).</p></td><td><p>Tulip 2.0 adds <strong>QR-based bill capture</strong> and <strong>encrypted JSON bulk diarisation</strong>, along with support for receiving bills in XML format to eliminate manual diarisation and enhance end-to-end connectivity. It is also ready to return passed-bill details in<strong> XML format</strong>.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>Merging Store/M/GeM/third-party bills and audit section change proposal.</p></td><td><p>As approved by <strong>CGDA (MoM dated 25.07.2024)</strong>, Stores &amp; Misc sections have been reorganized into Third-party Payment Section and Unit Payment Section. All imprest and public fund payments will be processed through the Unit Payment Section, while GeM bills will be handled by the Third-party Payment Section.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>Enhanced Randomization </p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, bill <strong>randomisation</strong> now uses SecureRandom from java.security within Spring Boot, providing stronger randomness and enhanced security. GO Level</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>Enhanced Logging Mechanism</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, application errors are auto-logged into date-wise log files, enabling easier monitoring and troubleshooting.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>Back Navigation Control</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, the browser back button is disabled to prevent data resubmission and navigation errors, ensuring smoother workflow and better security.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>Favourites Module Feature</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, users can mark commonly used modules as Favourites, which appear on the left panel after login for quicker, easier access.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>Analytical Dashboard</p></td><td><p>Tulip 2.0 includes a comprehensive dashboard that delivers analytical insights on budget and expenditure, enabling better monitoring and informed decision-making.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>Pending Tasks Panel</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, pending tasks appear on the right side of the landing page after login, helping users quickly view and prioritize their actions.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>Data Loss Prevention Alert</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, users receive a confirmation alert when refreshing, preventing accidental data loss and ensuring safer data handling.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>15</p></td><td><p>Global Exception Handling</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, a global exception handler captures all exceptions—caught or uncaught—and displays clear, user-friendly messages instead of raw JBoss errors or stack traces, greatly improving user experience and system professionalism.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>16</p></td><td><p>Medical Section – new features</p></td><td><p>The system auto-computes CGHS - based disallowances using standardized rates, supports section-wise cost calculations with manual entry options, and allows procedure updates through approved, time-stamped work flows. It generates a comprehensive disallowance report and offers a simple, user-friendly interface for faster, minimal-effort processing.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>17</p></td><td><p>Revamp of Civilian Pay section</p></td><td><p>The Civilian Pay section has been revamped with automation features similar to Tulip PMS, eliminating manual pay entry, unlinked demand recoveries, and the need for the Consolidated PM-CS.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>18</p></td><td><p>Roll Back </p></td><td><p>Before DP Sheet generation only.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>19</p></td><td><p>ECHS</p></td><td></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>Uniform Budget Checking across all modules like Bills, Medical, Transport.</p></td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td><p>An alert on clicking refresh, to confirm if it is intended action or accidental thus preventing losing data already entered.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>20</p></td><td><p>Creation of Vigilance &amp; Test Audit modules.</p></td><td><p>Planned for future implementation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>21</p></td><td><p>LAO Module</p></td><td><p>Planned for future implementation</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Sd/-</p><p>JCDA</p><p>ITSDC</p><p><strong>Annexure – C</strong></p><p><strong>Integration of Office Automation Projects (OAPs)</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Sl.</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>OAP Module</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Current Status</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>PDC</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Regional Controller Modules</p></td><td><p>As on date, Core Tulip (Regional Controller Modules) has been developed by IT&amp;SDC and ready to roll out</p></td><td><p>NA</p></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="3"><p>2</p></td><td><p>Functional Controller</p><p>Modules</p></td><td><p>Implemented in existing Tulip.</p></td><td><p>NA</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Navy &amp; Air force</p></td><td><p>Imprest Modules to be included in Tulip 2.0</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>IDS</p></td><td><p>Payment Authority Module to be included in Tulip 2.0</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>HAL </p></td><td><p>Inputs awaited from HAL Bengaluru</p></td><td><p>-</p></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2"><p>4</p></td><td rowspan="2"><p>Foreign Payments Module</p></td><td><p>Development Work is in progress and will be included in existing Tulip</p></td><td><p>01.01.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Roll out in Tulip 2.0 is planned</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Nodal Payments Module</p></td><td><p>Study of existing PHP programme is on-going.</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Fund Module</p></td><td><p>Taken care in Nidhi.</p></td><td><p>NA</p></td></tr></tbody></table>', 'D:\Admin_Sharing\Correspondence_    IT\TULIP_2.0\Annex - B & C - Tulip 2.0.docx', false, 1);
INSERT INTO public.document_pages VALUES (9, 8, '2026-07-03', 1, 'Imported Page 1', '<p><strong>No. IT&amp;SDC/Tulip 2.0/Corr								Annexure – B</strong></p><p><strong>Date: 24.11.2025</strong></p><p><strong>Changes in Tulip 2.0</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>S.no</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Functionalities in Tulip 2.0</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Current Status</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Technology Stack Upgrade</p></td><td><p>Tulip has been upgraded from Seam 2.2 to a modern, industry-standard stack using <strong>React JS and Spring Boot</strong>, delivering improved performance, scalability, and maintainability.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Hosting process and Tulip2.0 architecture:</p></td><td><p>Hosting will be done in a centralized manner, unlike the decentralized mode used in Tulip</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Centralized Master Data Management</p></td><td><p>Earlier, offices maintained separate local tables for Units, Vendors, Civil Employees and Bank details. These have now been unified into <strong>Central Unit, Vendor, Civil Employee and Bank Masters</strong> providing a single authoritative data source and ensuring seamless integration, consistency, and easier maintenance across all offices.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>Role-Based Authentication</p></td><td><p>Existing activity-based authentication required mapping each user to individual activities. Tulip 2.0 replaces this with a streamlined <strong>role-based</strong> authentication system, simplifying user management.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Redesigning R Section role; data capture at dak diarisation (bill intake).</p></td><td><p>Tulip 2.0 adds <strong>QR-based bill capture</strong> and <strong>encrypted JSON bulk diarisation</strong>, along with support for receiving bills in XML format to eliminate manual diarisation and enhance end-to-end connectivity. Development is underway to return passed-bill details in<strong> XML format</strong>.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Merging Store/M/GeM/third-party bills and audit section change proposal.</p></td><td><p>As approved by <strong>CGDA (MoM dated 25.07.2024)</strong>, Stores &amp; Misc sections have been reorganized into Third-party Payment Section and Unit Payment Section. All imprest and public fund payments will be processed through the Unit Payment Section, while GeM bills &amp; other third party bills will be handled by the Third-party Payment Section.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>Enhanced Randomization</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, bill <strong>randomisation</strong> now uses SecureRandom from java.security within Spring Boot, providing stronger randomness and enhanced security.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>8</p></td><td><p>Enhanced Logging Mechanism</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, application errors are auto-logged into date-wise log files, enabling easier monitoring and troubleshooting.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>9</p></td><td><p>Back Navigation Control</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, the browser back button is disabled to prevent data resubmission and navigation errors, ensuring smoother workflow and better security.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>10</p></td><td><p>‘Favourites’ module Feature</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, users can mark commonly used modules as Favourites, which appear on the left panel after login for quicker, easier access.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>11</p></td><td><p>Dashboard</p></td><td><p>Tulip 2.0 includes a comprehensive dashboard that provides analytical insights on budget and expenditure. Any additional details required to be displayed on the dashboard will be incorporated accordingly.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>12</p></td><td><p>Pending Tasks Panel</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, pending tasks appear on the right side of the landing page after login, helping users quickly view and prioritize their actions.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>13</p></td><td><p>Data Loss Prevention Alert</p></td><td><p>In Tulip 2.0, users receive a confirmation alert when refreshing, preventing accidental data loss and ensuring safer data handling.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>14</p></td><td><p>Medical Section – new features</p></td><td><p>The system auto-computes CGHS rates - based disallowances using standardized rates, and allows procedure updates through approved, time-stamped work flows. It generates a comprehensive disallowance report and offers a simple, user-friendly interface for faster, minimal-effort processing.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>15</p></td><td><p>Revamp of Civilian Pay section</p></td><td><p>The Civilian Pay section has been revamped with a centralized civilian employee structure, enabling the seamless transfer of pay details across various Controller offices whenever an employee moves to a different audit jurisdiction. The Civilian Pay Bill process flow has also been improved, making it significantly more user-friendly.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>16.</p></td><td><p> Budget Checking at Minor Head</p></td><td><p>Uniform Budget Checking at minor head level across all modules like Third Party Bills, Medical &amp; Transport.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>17</p></td><td><p>Creation of Vigilance &amp; Test Audit modules.</p></td><td><p>Planned for future implementation</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>18</p></td><td><p>LAO Module</p></td><td><p>Planned for future implementation</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>													       Sd/-</p><p>JCDA (IT&amp;SDC)</p>', 'D:\Admin_Sharing\Correspondence_    IT\TULIP_2.0\Audit Approvl\Changes in Tulip 2.0 - Annex.docx', false, 1);
INSERT INTO public.document_pages VALUES (10, 9, '2026-07-03', 1, 'Imported Page 1', '<p><strong>No. IT&amp;SDC/Tulip 2.0/Corr									Annexure – C</strong></p><p><strong>Date: 24.11.2025</strong></p><p><strong>Integration of Office Automation Projects (OAPs)</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th><p><strong>Sl.</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>OAP Module</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>Current Status</strong></p></th><th><p><strong>PDC</strong></p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Regional Controller, R&amp;D Modules</p></td><td><p>As on date, Core Tulip (Regional Controller Modules) has been developed by IT&amp;SDC and ready to roll out</p></td><td><p>NA</p></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2"><p>2</p></td><td><p>Navy &amp; Air force</p></td><td><p>Imprest Modules to be included in Tulip 2.0</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>IDS</p></td><td><p>Payment Authority Module to be included in Tulip 2.0</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>HAL </p></td><td><p>Inputs awaited from HAL Bengaluru.</p></td><td><p>-</p></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="2"><p>4</p></td><td rowspan="2"><p>Foreign Payments Module</p></td><td><p>Development Work is in progress and will be included in existing Tulip 1.0.</p></td><td><p>01.01.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>Roll out in Tulip 2.0 is planned</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Nodal Payments Module</p></td><td><p>Study of existing PHP programme is on-going.</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Fund Module</p></td><td><p>Development undertaken in Nidhi 2.0</p></td><td><p>NA</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>7</p></td><td><p>PCDA Kolkata Modules</p><p>1. Fund (Non-DAD)</p><p>2. Railway Claim</p><p>3. Railway Accounts</p><p>4. D Sn (SBI-CMP)</p><p>5. Record Section</p><p>6. Fin Comp Module</p><p>7. Transport/Medical/Pay</p><p>(Both DAD/Non-DAD)</p></td><td><p>In continuation of O/o the PCDA, Kolkata Letter No. 2379/IT&amp;S/Project/Training/Tulip dated 21.11.2025, wherein the OAPs proposed for integration into Tulip 2.0 were indicated, it is requested that a suitable representative from PCDA, Kolkata may please be deputed to this office to facilitate the provision of necessary inputs.</p></td><td><p>01.04.2026</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>		 Any other OAP can be included provided URS is given to ITSDC.</p><p>													Sd/-</p><p>												 JCDA(IT&amp;SDC)</p>', 'D:\Admin_Sharing\Correspondence_    IT\TULIP_2.0\Audit Approvl\Integration of OAPs - Annex.docx', false, 1);
